<!doctype html>
<!--
  The Orchard.

  Five trees standing in a quincunx — four at the corners of a square and one at
  its middle — with a guild of four plants under each, and meadow grass between
  them cut back into a disc round every trunk. It holds twenty plants where the
  Long Walk holds forty-eight, the Crossing twenty-four and the Quiet Garden ten,
  all in the same square.

  **The rule here is that one guild is finished before the next is begun.** It is
  the Crossing's rule turned inside out. There, an arriving plant goes wherever
  there is least, so that four ways meeting stay equally used; here it goes under
  the earliest tree with a place left, so that a tree is either dressed or bare
  and never one of five half-plantings. A young orchard has established trees and
  bare ones standing in the same row, and that unevenness is the thing this area
  exists to say.

  **The five trees belong to the garden, not to a gardener.** They are structures,
  as the Long Walk's hedges and the Quiet Garden's bench are, standing in every
  plot from the day it opens. This is the first area where the tallest thing in
  the plot is not something anybody grew — and the first where a plant stands
  under another thing rather than beside it.

  **This page is the one the app talks to, not a picture of it.** The plants are
  grown here, in the browser, from the same SeedCore that grows them on the
  phone — `plant.js` loads that library built for wasm32 and `orchard.js` hands
  it each planting the plot service holds. Nothing is drawn from an image and
  nothing is precomputed: a plant on this page is the plant on the phone because
  it is the same arithmetic, not because somebody kept two drawings in step. The
  trees come from the same place, through `Organic`.

  **The sky is the real one**, worked out for wherever this browser is keeping
  time and asking for nothing to find out — `sky.js`, a port of SeedCore's
  `Sky`, held to it by `tools/reference/check_sky.mjs`. Both halves of it: the
  plots float, so the stars under them are drawn too.

  **It is a night, so the page is dark whatever the reader's system says.**
  Every other page here follows `prefers-color-scheme`; this one cannot,
  because the garden is lit by its own sky and a pale page around it is a
  second room.

  `noindex`, for the reason `/g` gives: walkable and indexed are different
  properties and only one of them was asked for.

  Static, like the rest: no analytics, no font CDN, no third-party anything.
-->
<!-- `data-module` is stamped by index.php: the module's address with this
     build's mark on it, so a new one is a new address. -->
<html lang="en" data-module="PG_MODULE">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <title>Peace Garden — the Orchard</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Five trees in a quincunx, and the plants two people grew standing under them." />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/assets/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/assets/icon-180.png" />
  </head>

  <body class="night">
    <!--
      The plot itself, behind everything. The sky is behind it, and the pool of
      light sits between them so the plot stands in front of the sky rather than
      on top of a picture of one.
    -->
    <div class="walk" aria-hidden="true">
      <canvas id="sky"></canvas>
      <div class="pool"></div>
    </div>
    <canvas class="walk-stage" id="stage" aria-label="The Orchard"></canvas>

    <main class="page walk-page" id="page">
      <header class="masthead">
        <a href="/"
          ><img class="mark" src="/assets/icon.svg" alt="" width="44" height="44"
        /></a>
        <span class="wordmark">Peace Garden</span>
      </header>

      <h1 class="heading" data-s="areaKinship"></h1>
      <p class="body walk-about" data-s="orchardAbout"></p>

      <!--
        One line, and only when there is something to say: while the plants are
        being grown, or when there is nothing here yet. It carries no count — a
        running tally of plots and plants is a readout, and this is a garden.
      -->
      <p class="label walk-note" id="note" role="status" hidden></p>

      <nav class="walk-keys" id="keys" role="group" hidden>
        <button class="pad-key" type="button" id="back" data-s="walkBack"></button>
        <button class="pad-key" type="button" id="left" data-s="walkLeft"></button>
        <button class="pad-key" type="button" id="right" data-s="walkRight"></button>
        <button class="pad-key" type="button" id="on" data-s="walkOn"></button>
      </nav>

      <p class="notice body">
        <a href="/privacy" data-s="privacyTitle"></a>
      </p>

      <footer class="foot">
        <label class="chooser">
          <span class="label" id="language-label"></span>
          <span class="chooser__field">
            <select id="language" class="chooser__select"></select>
            <!-- Monoline, even weight, round free ends, per BRAND.md §3.2. -->
            <svg class="chooser__mark" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <path
                d="M4 6.5 L8 10.5 L12 6.5"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.25"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
              />
            </svg>
          </span>
        </label>
      </footer>
    </main>

    <script type="module" src="/assets/js/plain.js"></script>
    <script type="module" src="/assets/js/orchardpage.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
